{
  "about": "HTML pages in answers (pages.md, spec 3.8.0). `show` says what is asked. `fence`: a reply's `text` — expect `pages`, each closed `html-view` block in order with its `title` and its `html` (the lines between the fences, joined by newlines), and `projection`, the reply with every page replaced by its `[page: title]` line. `note`: a page's `title` — expect what a client that cannot render shows. `offered`: the `instance` switch, the `model`'s flag (absent: false), the `chat` switch, and `where` (absent: a chat; `scheduled`: a schedule's run on the server, which has no chat switch; `subagent`, `phone_assistant`, `agent_chat`) — expect whether the block is in the prompt. `note_line`: the chat's switch `change`d to `on` or `off` after the prompt was made — expect the session note's `line`. `static`: a page's `html` — expect `static` true, or false with `why`: what makes it not static, each once, in the order first met — `element:<name>` (not in pages.static.elements), `attribute:<name>` (not in pages.static.attributes, nor a kept prefix), `address:<attribute>` (an address other than #fragment or an inline data: image of a listed type), `css:import`, `css:url` (a url() that is neither) — names in lower case. It says what the rule is; a client still rebuilds the document with a real parser (pages.md §6). LLeMbas: services/pages.py; CLI: src/prototype/fence.ts.",
  "cases": [
    {
      "about": "A page with a title.",
      "show": "fence",
      "text": "Here are the sales.\n\n```html-view Monthly sales\n<!doctype html>\n<html><body><h1>Hi</h1></body></html>\n```\n\nThey rose.",
      "expect": {
        "pages": [
          {
            "title": "Monthly sales",
            "html": "<!doctype html>\n<html><body><h1>Hi</h1></body></html>"
          }
        ],
        "projection": "Here are the sales.\n\n[page: Monthly sales]\n\nThey rose."
      }
    },
    {
      "about": "No title on the line: the page's own <title>.",
      "show": "fence",
      "text": "```html-view\n<title>  Q3   results </title><p>x</p>\n```",
      "expect": {
        "pages": [
          {
            "title": "Q3 results",
            "html": "<title>  Q3   results </title><p>x</p>"
          }
        ],
        "projection": "[page: Q3 results]"
      }
    },
    {
      "about": "No title anywhere.",
      "show": "fence",
      "text": "```html-view\n<p>x</p>\n```",
      "expect": {
        "pages": [
          {
            "title": "Page",
            "html": "<p>x</p>"
          }
        ],
        "projection": "[page: Page]"
      }
    },
    {
      "about": "The word is exact: html is a code block, and so is html-views.",
      "show": "fence",
      "text": "```html\n<p>x</p>\n```\n\n```html-views A\n<p>y</p>\n```",
      "expect": {
        "pages": [],
        "projection": "```html\n<p>x</p>\n```\n\n```html-views A\n<p>y</p>\n```"
      }
    },
    {
      "about": "An unclosed fence is not a page.",
      "show": "fence",
      "text": "Look:\n\n```html-view Chart\n<svg>",
      "expect": {
        "pages": [],
        "projection": "Look:\n\n```html-view Chart\n<svg>"
      }
    },
    {
      "about": "Three backticks inside a page of four: the inner line does not end it.",
      "show": "fence",
      "text": "````html-view Code sample\n<pre>\n```js\nlet a = `x`\n```\n</pre>\n````\nafter",
      "expect": {
        "pages": [
          {
            "title": "Code sample",
            "html": "<pre>\n```js\nlet a = `x`\n```\n</pre>"
          }
        ],
        "projection": "[page: Code sample]\nafter"
      }
    },
    {
      "about": "A closing fence may be longer than the opening, not shorter.",
      "show": "fence",
      "text": "````html-view A\n<p>1</p>\n```\n<p>2</p>\n`````",
      "expect": {
        "pages": [
          {
            "title": "A",
            "html": "<p>1</p>\n```\n<p>2</p>"
          }
        ],
        "projection": "[page: A]"
      }
    },
    {
      "about": "Tildes are a fence too; backticks do not close it.",
      "show": "fence",
      "text": "~~~html-view Tilde\n<p>x</p>\n```\n~~~",
      "expect": {
        "pages": [
          {
            "title": "Tilde",
            "html": "<p>x</p>\n```"
          }
        ],
        "projection": "[page: Tilde]"
      }
    },
    {
      "about": "Two pages in one reply, and an ordinary code block between them left alone.",
      "show": "fence",
      "text": "```html-view One\n<p>1</p>\n```\n```js\nx()\n```\n   ```html-view   Two   words  \n<p>2</p>\n   ```",
      "expect": {
        "pages": [
          {
            "title": "One",
            "html": "<p>1</p>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Two words",
            "html": "<p>2</p>"
          }
        ],
        "projection": "[page: One]\n```js\nx()\n```\n[page: Two words]"
      }
    },
    {
      "about": "A page fence inside an ordinary code block is that block's text.",
      "show": "fence",
      "text": "````markdown\n```html-view Not one\n<p>x</p>\n```\n````",
      "expect": {
        "pages": [],
        "projection": "````markdown\n```html-view Not one\n<p>x</p>\n```\n````"
      }
    },
    {
      "about": "A long title is cut.",
      "show": "fence",
      "text": "```html-view tttttttttttttttttttttttttttttttttttttttttttttttttttttttttttttttttttttttttttttttttttttttttttttttttttt\n<p>x</p>\n```",
      "expect": {
        "pages": [
          {
            "title": "tttttttttttttttttttttttttttttttttttttttttttttttttttttttttttttttttttttttttttttttt",
            "html": "<p>x</p>"
          }
        ],
        "projection": "[page: tttttttttttttttttttttttttttttttttttttttttttttttttttttttttttttttttttttttttttttttt]"
      }
    },
    {
      "about": "The note a client that cannot render shows.",
      "show": "note",
      "title": "Monthly sales",
      "expect": {
        "note": "This answer has a page: Monthly sales"
      }
    },
    {
      "about": "All three on.",
      "show": "offered",
      "instance": true,
      "model": true,
      "chat": true,
      "expect": {
        "offered": true
      }
    },
    {
      "about": "The instance's switch off.",
      "show": "offered",
      "instance": false,
      "model": true,
      "chat": true,
      "expect": {
        "offered": false
      }
    },
    {
      "about": "The model cannot.",
      "show": "offered",
      "instance": true,
      "model": false,
      "chat": true,
      "expect": {
        "offered": false
      }
    },
    {
      "about": "The model says nothing: false.",
      "show": "offered",
      "instance": true,
      "chat": true,
      "expect": {
        "offered": false
      }
    },
    {
      "about": "The chat's switch off.",
      "show": "offered",
      "instance": true,
      "model": true,
      "chat": false,
      "expect": {
        "offered": false
      }
    },
    {
      "about": "A scheduled run has no chat switch: the instance and the model decide.",
      "show": "offered",
      "instance": true,
      "model": true,
      "where": "scheduled",
      "expect": {
        "offered": true
      }
    },
    {
      "about": "A scheduled run on an instance with the switch off.",
      "show": "offered",
      "instance": false,
      "model": true,
      "where": "scheduled",
      "expect": {
        "offered": false
      }
    },
    {
      "about": "Never to a subagent.",
      "show": "offered",
      "instance": true,
      "model": true,
      "chat": true,
      "where": "subagent",
      "expect": {
        "offered": false
      }
    },
    {
      "about": "Never in the phone assistant.",
      "show": "offered",
      "instance": true,
      "model": true,
      "chat": true,
      "where": "phone_assistant",
      "expect": {
        "offered": false
      }
    },
    {
      "about": "Never in an agent chat (a device, a terminal).",
      "show": "offered",
      "instance": true,
      "model": true,
      "chat": true,
      "where": "agent_chat",
      "expect": {
        "offered": false
      }
    },
    {
      "about": "A scheduled run on a linked computer is an agent chat: never.",
      "show": "offered",
      "instance": true,
      "model": true,
      "where": "agent_chat",
      "scheduled": true,
      "expect": {
        "offered": false
      }
    },
    {
      "about": "Switched on mid-chat: the note carries the block.",
      "show": "note_line",
      "change": "on",
      "pages_text": "- (the block)",
      "expect": {
        "line": "HTML pages are now on for this chat:\n- (the block)"
      }
    },
    {
      "about": "Switched off mid-chat.",
      "show": "note_line",
      "change": "off",
      "expect": {
        "line": "HTML pages are now off for this chat: write no more `html-view` blocks."
      }
    },
    {
      "about": "A static page: text, a table, a style element with the variables, inline SVG.",
      "show": "static",
      "html": "<!doctype html><html><head><title>Sales</title><style>body{color:var(--page-ink,#222);background:var(--page-bg,#fff)} td{border:1px solid var(--page-line,#ccc)}</style></head><body><h1>Sales</h1><table><tr><th scope=\"col\">Month</th><td colspan=\"2\">12</td></tr></table><svg viewBox=\"0 0 100 40\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Bars\"><rect x=\"0\" y=\"10\" width=\"20\" height=\"30\" fill=\"var(--page-accent,#06c)\"/><text x=\"10\" y=\"8\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"6\">12</text></svg></body></html>",
      "expect": {
        "static": true
      }
    },
    {
      "about": "A link within the page and an inline picture are the two addresses there are.",
      "show": "static",
      "html": "<a href=\"#totals\">Totals</a><h2 id=\"totals\">Totals</h2><img alt=\"dot\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,iVBORw0KGgo=\">",
      "expect": {
        "static": true
      }
    },
    {
      "about": "A script.",
      "show": "static",
      "html": "<p>x</p><script>fetch('https://example.org/')</script>",
      "expect": {
        "static": false,
        "why": [
          "element:script"
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "about": "An event handler.",
      "show": "static",
      "html": "<p onclick=\"go()\">x</p><svg onload=\"go()\"></svg>",
      "expect": {
        "static": false,
        "why": [
          "attribute:onclick",
          "attribute:onload"
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "about": "A link element — a dns-prefetch needs no script at all.",
      "show": "static",
      "html": "<link rel=\"dns-prefetch\" href=\"//example.org\"><p>x</p>",
      "expect": {
        "static": false,
        "why": [
          "element:link"
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "about": "meta, base, frames, objects, media, canvas, forms.",
      "show": "static",
      "html": "<meta http-equiv=\"refresh\" content=\"0;url=https://example.org\"><base href=\"https://example.org/\"><iframe src=\"https://example.org\"></iframe><object data=\"x\"></object><embed src=\"x\"><video src=\"x\"></video><audio></audio><canvas></canvas><form action=\"https://example.org\"><input name=\"q\"><button>go</button></form>",
      "expect": {
        "static": false,
        "why": [
          "element:meta",
          "element:base",
          "element:iframe",
          "element:object",
          "element:embed",
          "element:video",
          "element:audio",
          "element:canvas",
          "element:form",
          "element:input",
          "element:button"
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "about": "An address that leaves the page.",
      "show": "static",
      "html": "<a href=\"https://example.org/\">out</a><img src=\"https://example.org/p.png\" alt=\"\"><a href=\"page2.html\">next</a>",
      "expect": {
        "static": false,
        "why": [
          "address:href",
          "address:src"
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "about": "A javascript: address, a protocol-relative one, a data: address that is not a picture, an SVG picture.",
      "show": "static",
      "html": "<a href=\"JavaScript:go()\">x</a><a href=\"//example.org\">y</a><a href=\"data:text/html;base64,PGI+\">z</a><img alt=\"\" src=\"data:image/svg+xml;base64,PHN2Zz4=\">",
      "expect": {
        "static": false,
        "why": [
          "address:href",
          "address:src"
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "about": "CSS that would fetch: @import and url() to anywhere; url(#id) and an inline picture are fine.",
      "show": "static",
      "html": "<style>@import url(https://example.org/a.css); .a{background:url(https://example.org/b.png)} .b{fill:url(#grad)} .c{background:url(data:image/png;base64,iVBOR=)}</style><p style=\"background:url('//example.org/c.png')\">x</p>",
      "expect": {
        "static": false,
        "why": [
          "css:import",
          "css:url"
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "about": "Elements and attributes nobody listed: dropped, whatever they are.",
      "show": "static",
      "html": "<marquee>x</marquee><template><p>y</p></template><svg><foreignObject><p>z</p></foreignObject><use href=\"#a\"/></svg><p contenteditable=\"true\" data-n=\"1\" aria-hidden=\"true\">w</p>",
      "expect": {
        "static": false,
        "why": [
          "element:marquee",
          "element:template",
          "element:foreignobject",
          "attribute:contenteditable"
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "about": "An xlink:href is not a listed attribute; a use that points outside is an address.",
      "show": "static",
      "html": "<svg><use xlink:href=\"#a\"/><use href=\"https://example.org/s.svg#a\"/></svg>",
      "expect": {
        "static": false,
        "why": [
          "attribute:xlink:href",
          "address:href"
        ]
      }
    }
  ]
}
